{%- comment %}
============ PROTOTYPE: FACT + FLAVOUR ============
Two lines instead of one. The fact line is built from short templates,
a few wordings per situation, and is the same at every sarcasm level. The flavour
line carries the personality: picked by the mood of the day, never
asked to carry a fact, absent at sarcasm 0.

Inserted by prototypes/fact-flavour/build.py ahead of THE PICTURE,
after the old hint is built, so both can be rendered side by side.
Reads only what the scenario logic above already worked out.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign fact_line = '' -%}
{%- assign flavour_line = '' -%}
{%- assign mood = '' -%}
{%- assign now_mood = '' -%}
{%- assign fl_now_pool = nil -%}
{%- assign flavour_topical = false -%}
{%- comment %}
The two switches (config/settings.next.yaml):
  Forecast            show_future_suggestions, the field that was there:
                      "Yes"/"No" saved before, true/false now. The words.
  What to Wear Next?  what_to_wear_next, true/false: the drawings.
Both can be on. The first beta had the drawings as a third Forecast value,
"visual": a fork with that saved keeps drawings without words.
The sarcastic line no longer needs either: it shows at On and 11 even on
the outfit alone.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign forecast_on = false -%}
{%- if show_future_suggestions == 'on' and sfs_check != 'visual' -%}{%- assign forecast_on = true -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- assign next_check = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.what_to_wear_next | append: '' | downcase | strip -%}
{%- assign next_on = false -%}
{%- if next_check == 'true' or next_check == 'on' or next_check == 'yes' or next_check == '1' or sfs_check == 'visual' -%}
  {%- assign next_on = true -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- comment %}
Which wording shows changes every hour, not once a day, so a day whose
weather doesn't change still reads differently in the afternoon. Each
pool takes (text_rot + its own offset) mod its size. Day and hour are
multiplied by primes larger than any pool (101, 103: coprime with every
size up to 100), so each step lands somewhere else in the pool instead
of on the next line, every line comes round, and someone who looks at
7:00 every morning sees the whole pool over the days, not a subset.
The screen changes when TRMNL next regenerates it: the weather's
current time moves every 15 minutes, so the merge variables change.
{%- endcomment %}
{%- assign text_rot = local_days | times: 101 -%}
{%- assign text_rot_h = local_hour | times: 103 -%}
{%- assign text_rot = text_rot | plus: text_rot_h -%}
{%- if is_error == false and texts_ok and texts.facts -%}
  {%- assign F = texts.facts -%}
  {%- if is_steady -%}
    {%- if local_hour >= 17 -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady_evening' -%}
    {%- elsif band_rank >= 7 -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady_hot' -%}
    {%- elsif band_rank <= 2 -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady_cold' -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign f_key = 'steady' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign f_key = temp_scenario -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %}
  The garment on screen, for the arc keys: {G} the garment, {GP} its
  pronoun, {GV} garment with its verb (German agrees "kann"/"können").
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign f_g = '' -%}
  {%- assign f_gp = '' -%}
  {%- assign f_gv = '' -%}
  {%- if band_rank <= 4 -%}
    {%- assign fgi = band_rank | minus: 1 -%}
    {%- assign f_g = F.garments[fgi] -%}
    {%- assign f_gp = F.garments_pron[fgi] -%}
    {%- assign f_gv = F.garments_verb[fgi] -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %}
  Each situation has several wordings, rotated by the hour like the
  flavour line (text_rot) but on their own offsets, so a run of the same
  weather doesn't show the same words.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign f_temp = '' -%}
  {%- assign f_list = F[f_key] -%}
  {%- if f_list -%}
    {%- assign f_n = f_list | size -%}
    {%- assign f_vi = text_rot | plus: 2 | modulo: f_n -%}
    {%- assign f_temp = f_list[f_vi] -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign f_temp = f_temp | replace: '{GV}', f_gv | replace: '{GP}', f_gp | replace: '{G}', f_g -%}
  {%- assign f_temp = f_temp | replace: '{WHEN2}', when_temp2 | replace: '{WHEN}', when_temp -%}
  {%- assign f_precip = '' -%}
  {%- if precip_scenario != '' -%}
    {%- assign pk = 'p_' | append: precip_scenario -%}
    {%- comment %} Snowing now: the snow wording, where the situation has one. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- if is_now_snow == 1 -%}
      {%- assign pks = pk | append: '_snow' -%}
      {%- if F[pks] -%}{%- assign pk = pks -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- assign p_list = F[pk] -%}
    {%- if p_list -%}
      {%- assign p_n = p_list | size -%}
      {%- assign p_vi = text_rot | plus: 3 | modulo: p_n -%}
      {%- assign f_precip = p_list[p_vi] | replace: '{WHENP}', when_precip -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if is_steady and f_precip != '' -%}
    {%- assign fact_line = f_precip -%}
  {%- elsif f_precip != '' -%}
    {%- assign fact_line = f_temp | append: ' ' | append: f_precip -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign fact_line = f_temp -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- assign fact_line = fact_line | replace: '  ', ' ' | replace: ' .', '.' | replace: ' ,', ',' | strip -%}
  {%- assign marked = fact_line | replace: '. ', '.^^' | replace: '! ', '!^^' | replace: '? ', '?^^' -%}
  {%- assign sentences = marked | split: '^^' -%}
  {%- assign cased = '' -%}
  {%- for sentence in sentences -%}
    {%- assign s = sentence | strip -%}
    {%- assign head = s | slice: 0 | upcase -%}
    {%- assign tail = s | slice: 1, 400 -%}
    {%- if forloop.first -%}
      {%- assign cased = head | append: tail -%}
    {%- else -%}
      {%- assign cased = cased | append: ' ' | append: head | append: tail -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
  {%- assign fact_line = cased -%}

  {%- comment %} The mood of the day, for the flavour line. First match wins. {%- endcomment %}
  {%- assign temp_prefix = temp_scenario | slice: 0, 2 -%}
  {%- if precip_scenario == 'snow_coming' or is_now_snow == 1 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'snow' -%}
  {%- elsif precip_scenario != '' -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'wet' -%}
  {%- elsif is_steady and local_hour >= 22 -%}
    {%- comment %} Only this late may a line mention bed: at 19:00 people check before going out. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'night' -%}
  {%- elsif is_steady and local_hour >= 18 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'evening' -%}
  {%- elsif is_arc and temp_scenario != 'arc_warmer' -%}
    {%- comment %}
    Only an arc that wants the layer back. When the evening stays warmer
    than the morning, the fact says "can come off and stay off", and
    "Erst zu warm, dann zu kalt" or "An, aus, wieder an" would contradict
    it: that day falls through to hot or warming.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'fickle' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank >= 7 or up_rank >= 7 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'hot' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank <= 2 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'cold' -%}
  {%- elsif is_steady and band_rank >= 4 -%}
    {%- assign mood = 'nice' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_prefix == 'c_' -%}
    {%- comment %} An ordinary day, split by what it actually does: a layer is needed later... {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'cooling' -%}
  {%- elsif temp_scenario != '' -%}
    {%- comment %} ...something comes off later (the commonest of all)... {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'warming' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment %} ...or a steady, cool jacket day. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign mood = 'cool' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- comment %}
  What the Now drawing shows, for the "now" lines (now_10 / now_11): they
  stand alone and agree with the drawing, so they fit every screen, the
  outfit alone included. Rain and snow only while they fall: that's when
  the drawing has them.
  {%- endcomment %}
  {%- if is_now_snow == 1 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'snow' -%}
  {%- elsif is_now_precip == 1 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'wet' -%}
  {%- elsif local_hour >= 22 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'night' -%}
  {%- elsif local_hour >= 18 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'evening' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank >= 7 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'hot' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank <= 2 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'cold' -%}
  {%- elsif band_rank >= 4 -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'nice' -%}
  {%- else -%}
    {%- assign now_mood = 'cool' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if sarcasm_level != '0' -%}
    {%- assign fl_key = 'flavour_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign fl_lib = texts[fl_key] -%}
    {%- assign now_key = 'now_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign fl_now_pool = texts[now_key][now_mood] -%}
    {%- unless fl_now_pool -%}{%- assign fl_now_pool = fl_lib[now_mood] -%}{%- endunless -%}
    {%- comment %}
    The day's lines (the mood's pool) are about the shape of the day: a
    change, or a day without one ("Easy day to forecast"). They join when
    that's true on screen: the forecast line on a day that changes, or a
    steady day. Then they mix with the now lines. Two or three drawings
    without words get theirs in the panels block. Otherwise: now lines.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign fl_pool = fl_now_pool -%}
    {%- assign fl_day_pool = fl_lib[mood] -%}
    {%- assign fl_day_shown = is_steady -%}
    {%- if forecast_on and fact_line != '' -%}{%- assign fl_day_shown = true -%}{%- endif -%}
    {%- if fl_day_shown and fl_day_pool -%}
      {%- if fl_now_pool -%}
        {%- assign fl_pool = fl_day_pool | concat: fl_now_pool -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign fl_pool = fl_day_pool -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment %} A seasonal day with nothing else to say gets its own lines. {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign fl_theme = false -%}
    {%- if is_steady and active_theme != '' -%}
      {%- assign th_key = 'theme_' | append: active_theme -%}
      {%- if fl_lib[th_key] -%}
        {%- assign fl_pool = fl_lib[th_key] -%}
        {%- assign fl_theme = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if fl_pool -%}
      {%- assign fl_n = fl_pool | size -%}
      {%- assign fl_i = text_rot | plus: 5 | modulo: fl_n -%}
      {%- assign flavour_line = fl_pool[fl_i] -%}
    {%- endif -%}

    {%- comment %}
    ============ TOPICAL LINES ============
    Lines about current events, written with the owner and voted like the
    rest (.claude/skills/topical). Each carries a window and shows only
    inside it, so an expired line needs no republish; tools/topical.py
    prunes it from the file later.

      {"text": "...", "from": "2026-10-25", "until": "2026-10-29",
       "region": "UK,IE", "moods": "cold,wet"}

    region and moods are optional. A line shows on the first day of its
    window and then about one day in three, rotating with whatever else
    is active; the other days keep the mood's line, so a week of one joke
    doesn't wear thin. A seasonal theme day keeps its own lines. Off
    unless the topical_lines field is "on": installs from before the field
    have no value, so they never see news they didn't ask for.
    {%- endcomment %}
    {%- assign topical_raw = trmnl.plugin_settings.custom_fields_values.topical_lines | default: 'off' | downcase | strip -%}
    {%- assign tp_key = 'topical_' | append: sarcasm_level -%}
    {%- assign tp_list = texts[tp_key] -%}
    {%- if topical_raw == 'on' and fl_theme == false and tp_list -%}
      {%- comment %}
      Region from the forecast's own time zone (Open-Meteo, timezone=auto),
      which follows the device's location, not the account's.
      {%- endcomment %}
      {%- if IDX_0 -%}{%- assign tp_tz = IDX_0.timezone | default: '' -%}{%- else -%}{%- assign tp_tz = timezone | default: '' -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- assign tp_probe = ',' | append: tp_tz | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign tp_region = '' -%}
      {%- assign US_ZONES = ',America/New_York,America/Chicago,America/Denver,America/Los_Angeles,America/Phoenix,America/Anchorage,America/Detroit,America/Boise,America/Juneau,America/Sitka,America/Nome,America/Yakutat,America/Metlakatla,America/Adak,America/Menominee,Pacific/Honolulu,' -%}
      {%- if tp_probe == ',Europe/Berlin,' or tp_probe == ',Europe/Busingen,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'DE' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/Vienna,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'AT' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/Zurich,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'CH' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/London,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'UK' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_probe == ',Europe/Dublin,' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'IE' -%}
      {%- elsif US_ZONES contains tp_probe or tp_tz contains 'America/Indiana/' or tp_tz contains 'America/Kentucky/' or tp_tz contains 'America/North_Dakota/' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'US' -%}
      {%- elsif tp_tz contains 'Australia/' -%}
        {%- assign tp_region = 'AU' -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- assign tp_region_probe = ',' | append: tp_region | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign tp_mood_probe = ',' | append: mood | append: ',' -%}
      {%- assign tp_today = today_year | append: '-' | append: today_md -%}
      {%- assign tp_cycle = local_days | modulo: 3 -%}
      {%- assign tp_joined = '' -%}
      {%- assign tp_n = 0 -%}
      {%- for t in tp_list -%}
        {%- if t.from <= tp_today and t.until >= tp_today -%}
          {%- assign tp_ok = true -%}
          {%- if t.region and t.region != '' -%}
            {%- assign tp_regions = ',' | append: t.region | remove: ' ' | append: ',' -%}
            {%- unless tp_region != '' and tp_regions contains tp_region_probe -%}{%- assign tp_ok = false -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if t.moods and t.moods != '' -%}
            {%- assign tp_moods = ',' | append: t.moods | remove: ' ' | append: ',' -%}
            {%- unless tp_moods contains tp_mood_probe -%}{%- assign tp_ok = false -%}{%- endunless -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- if tp_ok and t.from == tp_today or tp_ok and tp_cycle == 0 -%}
            {%- if tp_n == 0 -%}
              {%- assign tp_joined = t.text -%}
            {%- else -%}
              {%- assign tp_joined = tp_joined | append: '~|~' | append: t.text -%}
            {%- endif -%}
            {%- assign tp_n = tp_n | plus: 1 -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
      {%- if tp_n > 0 -%}
        {%- assign tp_texts = tp_joined | split: '~|~' -%}
        {%- assign tp_i = local_days | divided_by: 3 | modulo: tp_n -%}
        {%- assign flavour_line = tp_texts[tp_i] -%}
        {%- assign flavour_topical = true -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
